{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L226","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:226"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convention for tool-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" that marks a call as "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider-executed"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n— run by the provider's own infrastructure (e.g. Anthropic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"web_search"},{"type":"text","value":" /\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"web_fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" server tools) rather than by the agent loop. Adapters set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerExecuted: true"},{"type":"text","value":" so that:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The agent loop never tries to execute the call client-side (see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../functions/isProviderExecutedToolCall.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"isProviderExecutedToolCall"}]},{"type":"text","value":" usage in the chat engine), and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter can stash the raw provider result alongside it so the call —\nand its evidence — round-trips into the next turn's request."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-specific payloads live under a namespaced key (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anthropic"},{"type":"text","value":"),\nkeeping this convention opaque to the framework core. The index signature\npreserves those per-adapter fields. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sources"},{"type":"text","value":" is the normalized list of\nlinks a web search used, shared across providers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"indexable","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Indexable"}]},{"type":"code","value":"[key: string]: unknown","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"providerexecuted","children":[{"type":"text","value":"providerExecuted?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional providerExecuted?: boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L227","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:227"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sources?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional sources?: ProviderExecutedToolSource[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L228","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:228"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"indexable","text":"Indexable","level":2},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"providerexecuted","text":"providerExecuted?","level":3},{"id":"sources","text":"sources?","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:226](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L226)\n\nConvention for tool-call `metadata` that marks a call as **provider-executed**\n— run by the provider's own infrastructure (e.g. Anthropic `web_search` /\n`web_fetch` server tools) rather than by the agent loop. Adapters set\n`providerExecuted: true` so that:\n\n1. The agent loop never tries to execute the call client-side (see\n   [isProviderExecutedToolCall](../functions/isProviderExecutedToolCall.md) usage in the chat engine), and\n2. The adapter can stash the raw provider result alongside it so the call —\n   and its evidence — round-trips into the next turn's request.\n\nProvider-specific payloads live under a namespaced key (e.g. `anthropic`),\nkeeping this convention opaque to the framework core. The index signature\npreserves those per-adapter fields. `sources` is the normalized list of\nlinks a web search used, shared across providers.\n\n## Indexable\n\n```ts\n[key: string]: unknown\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### providerExecuted?\n\n```ts\noptional providerExecuted?: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:227](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L227)\n\n***\n\n### sources?\n\n```ts\noptional sources?: ProviderExecutedToolSource[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:228](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L228)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ProviderExecutedToolMetadata\ntitle: ProviderExecutedToolMetadata\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:226](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L226)\n\nConvention for tool-call `metadata` that marks a call as **provider-executed**\n— run by the provider's own infrastructure (e.g. Anthropic `web_search` /\n`web_fetch` server tools) rather than by the agent loop. Adapters set\n`providerExecuted: true` so that:\n\n1. The agent loop never tries to execute the call client-side (see\n   [isProviderExecutedToolCall](../functions/isProviderExecutedToolCall.md) usage in the chat engine), and\n2. The adapter can stash the raw provider result alongside it so the call —\n   and its evidence — round-trips into the next turn's request.\n\nProvider-specific payloads live under a namespaced key (e.g. `anthropic`),\nkeeping this convention opaque to the framework core. The index signature\npreserves those per-adapter fields. `sources` is the normalized list of\nlinks a web search used, shared across providers.\n\n## Indexable\n\n```ts\n[key: string]: unknown\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### providerExecuted?\n\n```ts\noptional providerExecuted?: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:227](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L227)\n\n***\n\n### sources?\n\n```ts\noptional sources?: ProviderExecutedToolSource[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:228](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L228)\n"}
